{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788374345120,"sessionID":"ses_f9c952882ffeAnIEP58bPaIy7l","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"skill","callID":"call_a87e9335592b4f619e35c882","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"name":"pyasc-cannbench-kernel"},"output":"<skill_content name=\"pyasc-cannbench-kernel\">\n# Skill: pyasc-cannbench-kernel\n\n# pyasc v2 CANNBench kernel workflow\n\nUse this skill only for the vendored benchmark under\n`integrations/cannbench/`. Its compact module contract overrides the generic\nstandalone-kernel workflow.\n\n## Non-negotiable contract\n\n- Treat `tasks/<op>/proto.yaml`, `golden.py`, and all 20 entries in\n  `cases.yaml` as one indivisible specification.\n- Produce one `candidate.py` with the exact top-level callable and defaults.\n- Use `torch` only for allocation, metadata views, and launches. Numerical work\n  belongs in one or more `@asc2.jit` kernels.\n- Import and call `ensure_npu_platform` from `._pyasc_runtime`.\n- Target `Ascend950PR_9599`, at most 72 vector cores, and UB capacity 253952 B.\n- For the pinned runtime use `asc2.global_tensor`, `asc2.copy_in`, and\n  `asc2.copy_out`; use `real_shape` for tails. Do not substitute the older\n  `tensor/load/store` spelling.\n- Treat padded lanes as executed lanes: choose an explicit, operation-neutral\n  `pad_value` for `real_shape` loads (especially `1` for divisors) so tail\n  arithmetic does not create avoidable Inf/NaN exceptions.\n- A production candidate normally uses bare `@asc2.jit` or an evidenced\n  allocation option. `always_compile=True` is a development aid, not a\n  submission requirement.\n\n## Required workflow\n\n1. Read the three task files and summarize every dtype, rank, attribute, list\n   arity, special value, and boundary shape. Do not optimize for one example.\n   An upstream target test is a useful implementation reference, not evidence\n   that its narrower dtype/shape/attribute domain implements this contract.\n2. Read [operator patterns](references/operator-patterns.md), selecting only\n   the target operator section.\n3. Design host dispatch, kernel specializations, tails, dtype conversions, UB\n   budget, and numerical behavior before writing code.\n4. Implement the exact callable. Run `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` and\n   the worker static contract check.\n5. Run the exact-v2 local compile gate for that operator as described in\n   [local validation](references/local-validation.md). A compile failure is\n   measured feedback; repair it and re-run all 20 cases.\n6. For numerically sensitive formulas, run the adversarial camodel smoke when\n   the native runtime is available. It must exercise both ordinary and\n   special-value routes using the task's dtype-specific tolerances. Treat a\n   small all-finite smoke as insufficient for promotion.\n7. Have a different available model review the task, design, candidate, and\n   local report. Record both model IDs, OpenCode session IDs, loaded skill\n   source hashes, prompt/design/candidate hashes, and gate results.\n\nNever claim numerical correctness or performance from the local compile gate.\nOnly camodel execution can provide local numerical evidence; only CANNBench on\nthe real NPU is the acceptance/performance oracle.\n\n## Evidence labels\n\nUse exactly one label for every conclusion:\n\n- `verified-local-compile`: all task routes lower through pinned pyasc v2.\n- `verified-camodel-smoke`: the stated representative routes executed and\n  matched their golden; scope must list omitted dtypes/shapes/cases.\n- `verified-camodel`: outputs were executed and compared to the task golden.\n- `verified-cannbench`: official hardware result and case count are recorded.\n- `suspected`: evidence is incomplete or the root cause is inferred.\n\nDo not promote a locally qualified candidate into the canonical submission\npackage without numerical evidence. When a CANNBench run reports case-level\nfailures, feed those exact case IDs and failure classes into repair; a clean\ncompile matrix must never override measured numerical failures. Do not spend a\nsubmission credit unless the user explicitly enables remote evaluation.\n\n## Known limitations\n\nBefore using a workaround, consult\n[pyasc v2 blockers](references/pyasc-v2-blockers.md). Preserve full case\ncoverage when a case exposes a compiler limit; never remove or shrink the case\nto make a gate pass.\n\nBase directory for this skill: /home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n<file>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/local-validation.md</file>\n<file>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/pyasc-v2-blockers.md</file>\n<file>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/operator-patterns.md</file>\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>","metadata":{"name":"pyasc-cannbench-kernel","dir":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel","truncated":false},"title":"Loaded skill: pyasc-cannbench-kernel","time":{"start":1788374345112,"end":1788374345119}},"id":"prt_0636ae49a001W6Yj4zWmeVhclh","sessionID":"ses_f9c952882ffeAnIEP58bPaIy7l","messageID":"msg_0636ad84c001qK5pwkwH9hce0x"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788374345831,"sessionID":"ses_f9c952882ffeAnIEP58bPaIy7l","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_92c39c9ad3bd4f16b1be1082","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/task.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/task.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Repair task: CANNBench GELU after real 950PR feedback\n2: \n3: Repair `candidate.py` for the vendored CANNBench GELU contract. Numerical work\n4: must remain in pyasc v2 `@asc2.jit` kernels and the public signature remains\n5: `gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n6: \n7: The candidate already passes the exact-v2 compile matrix, but private 950PR job\n8: `job_ae3bfdefd087` passed only 16/20. All failures are FP32 precision failures:\n9: \n10: - case 5, tanh, range [-100, 100]: MERE 9.008301e-4;\n11: - case 8, tanh, range [-5, 10]: MERE 0.003110;\n12: - case 11, exact, range [-88, 88]: MERE 0.002386;\n13: - case 20, exact, range [-20, 40]: MERE 0.006894.\n14: \n15: BF16 Inf/NaN case 12 passes in this seed and must remain passing. The direct\n16: `1 + erf/tanh` forms cancel in negative tails. Apply the updated\n17: `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` skill's 950PR-verified stable GELU formulations. Do not\n18: copy or inspect the repository's canonical submission implementation. Preserve\n19: all dtypes, tails, attributes and special-value semantics. After editing, run\n20: only `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` and end with `REPAIR_DONE`.\n21: \n22: The first repair attempt is rejected. It substituted a different\n23: Abramowitz-Stegun-style polynomial, evaluated it at `abs(x)` instead of\n24: `abs(x)/sqrt(2)`, and did not implement the required Numerical Recipes Horner\n25: chain. Replace that rejected exact-mode body using the now-explicit coefficient\n26: sequence in the skill reference; do not merely review it for syntax.\n27: \n28: The second repair attempt implemented the required formula, but the exact-v2\n29: compile gate rejected every exact-mode specialization. With\n30: `tile_size=2048`, `unroll_factor=2`, reported UB use is 819968 bytes for\n31: FP16/BF16 and 795392 bytes for FP32, above the 253952-byte limit. The three\n32: tanh specializations pass at tile 1024 and use 172032--184320 bytes. Apply the\n33: updated measured tile rule from the skill reference: exact mode must use the\n34: safe 512-element tile with unroll factor 2. Keep the stable formulas and do not\n35: regress the already-passing tanh branch.\n\n(End of file - total 35 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Repair task: CANNBench GELU after real 950PR feedback\n\nRepair `candidate.py` for the vendored CANNBench GELU contract. Numerical work\nmust remain in pyasc v2 `@asc2.jit` kernels and the public signature remains\n`gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n\nThe candidate already passes the exact-v2 compile matrix, but private 950PR job\n`job_ae3bfdefd087` passed only 16/20. All failures are FP32 precision failures:\n\n- case 5, tanh, range [-100, 100]: MERE 9.008301e-4;\n- case 8, tanh, range [-5, 10]: MERE 0.003110;\n- case 11, exact, range [-88, 88]: MERE 0.002386;\n- case 20, exact, range [-20, 40]: MERE 0.006894.\n\nBF16 Inf/NaN case 12 passes in this seed and must remain passing. The direct\n`1 + erf/tanh` forms cancel in negative tails. Apply the updated\n`pyasc-cannbench-kernel` skill's 950PR-verified stable GELU formulations. Do not\ncopy or inspect the repository's canonical submission implementation. Preserve\nall dtypes, tails, attributes and special-value semantics. After editing, run\nonly `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` and end with `REPAIR_DONE`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/task.md","text":"# Repair task: CANNBench GELU after real 950PR feedback\n\nRepair `candidate.py` for the vendored CANNBench GELU contract. Numerical work\nmust remain in pyasc v2 `@asc2.jit` kernels and the public signature remains\n`gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n\nThe candidate already passes the exact-v2 compile matrix, but private 950PR job\n`job_ae3bfdefd087` passed only 16/20. All failures are FP32 precision failures:\n\n- case 5, tanh, range [-100, 100]: MERE 9.008301e-4;\n- case 8, tanh, range [-5, 10]: MERE 0.003110;\n- case 11, exact, range [-88, 88]: MERE 0.002386;\n- case 20, exact, range [-20, 40]: MERE 0.006894.\n\nBF16 Inf/NaN case 12 passes in this seed and must remain passing. The direct\n`1 + erf/tanh` forms cancel in negative tails. Apply the updated\n`pyasc-cannbench-kernel` skill's 950PR-verified stable GELU formulations. Do not\ncopy or inspect the repository's canonical submission implementation. Preserve\nall dtypes, tails, attributes and special-value semantics. After editing, run\nonly `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` and end with `REPAIR_DONE`.\n\nThe first repair attempt is rejected. It substituted a different\nAbramowitz-Stegun-style polynomial, evaluated it at `abs(x)` instead of\n`abs(x)/sqrt(2)`, and did not implement the required Numerical Recipes Horner\nchain. Replace that rejected exact-mode body using the now-explicit coefficient\nsequence in the skill reference; do not merely review it for syntax.\n\nThe second repair attempt implemented the required formula, but the exact-v2\ncompile gate rejected every exact-mode specialization. With\n`tile_size=2048`, `unroll_factor=2`, reported UB use is 819968 bytes for\nFP16/BF16 and 795392 bytes for FP32, above the 253952-byte limit. The three\ntanh specializations pass at tile 1024 and use 172032--184320 bytes. Apply the\nupdated measured tile rule from the skill reference: exact mode must use the\nsafe 512-element tile with unroll factor 2. Keep the stable formulas and do not\nregress the already-passing tanh branch.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":35,"totalLines":35,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/task.md","time":{"start":1788374345819,"end":1788374345828}},"id":"prt_0636ae5f6001i215QicW04PCZ3","sessionID":"ses_f9c952882ffeAnIEP58bPaIy7l","messageID":"msg_0636ad84c001qK5pwkwH9hce0x"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788374346504,"sessionID":"ses_f9c952882ffeAnIEP58bPaIy7l","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_b71820e1152f42d6b86a92de","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/design.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/design.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # design.md — Gelu (CANNBench, pyasc asc2)\n2: \n3: Provenance: skills `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` + `pyasc-syntax-constraints` loaded; context\n4: = `task.md` (desc/proto/golden/20 cases + kernel contract) only. No submission modules,\n5: run artifacts, or pyasc source inspected. `candidate.py` not yet written.\n6: \n7: ## 1. Algorithm\n8: \n9: Public callable `gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n10: `approximate` is a **str** → unsupported as a kernel param (type constraints).\n11: Dispatch on the host string and launch one of two specialized `@asc2.jit` kernels.\n12: Both kernels flatten to 1-D (`numel`), promote f16/bf16→f32, compute, cast back.\n13: \n14: - **erf mode** (`approximate == \"none\"`): `y = (x*0.5) * (erf(x*C1) + 1.0)`,\n15:   `C1 = 1/sqrt(2) = 0.7071067811865476`.\n16: - **tanh mode** (`approximate == \"tanh\"`):\n17:   `y = (x*0.5) * (tanh(C0 * (x + K*x*x*x)) + 1.0)`,\n18:   `C0 = sqrt(2/pi) = 0.7978845608028654`, `K = 0.044715`.\n19:   Compute order: `x2=x*x; x3=x2*x; a=x3*K; b=x+a; c=b*C0; t=tanh(c); one=t+1.0; hx=x*0.5; y=hx*one`.\n20: \n21: All constants are module-level floats (no `math.*` inside jit). Scalars always on the\n22: RIGHT of tile arithmetic (`x*C1`, `t+1.0`, `x*0.5`) — `Tile.__rmul__` is absent.\n23: \n24: ## 2. Pinned v2 APIs (CANNBench contract)\n25: \n26: - `from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform`\n27: - `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` — 1-D GM view (rank-1 throughout; no 2-D mix).\n28: - `asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile], real_shape=[n])` — tile load with tail.\n29: - `asc2.copy_out(y_cast, out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])` — tile store with tail.\n30: - `asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2)` — grid-stride.\n31: - `asc.GlobalAddress` for ptrs; `int` for size/num_tiles; `asc.ConstExpr[int]` for tile size.\n32: - Casts: `x.to(asc.float32)`, `y.to(x.dtype)`. Math: `asc2.erf`, `asc2.tanh`, `+ *`.\n33: - Launch: `kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, TILE)` with `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`.\n34: - Target: `Ascend950PR_9599`, 72 AIV cores, UB 253952 B.\n35: \n36: ## 3. All 20 cases (coverage)\n37: \n38: 1-D flatten + grid-stride + `real_shape` tails covers every rank (1D–5D present;\n39: spec 0–8D) and every odd/non-multiple shape. No host shape branch needed.\n40: \n41: | # | shape | dtype | range | mode | elems | path |\n42: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n43: |1|[1024,1024]|f16|[-1,1]|erf|1.05M|erf|\n44: |2|[2048,2048]|f32|[-2,2]|erf|4.19M|erf|\n45: |3|[4096,4096]|bf16|[-3,3]|erf|16.78M|erf|\n46: |4|[8192,8192]|f16|[-10,10]|tanh|67.1M|tanh|\n47: |5|[8192,8192]|f32|[-100,100]|tanh|67.1M|tanh|\n48: |6|[1023,1023]|bf16|[-0.1,0.1]|tanh|1.05M|tanh|\n49: |7|[1009,1021]|f16|[-1,2]|erf|1.03M|erf|\n50: |8|[1537,769]|f32|[-5,10]|tanh|1.18M|tanh|\n51: |9|[363,367,373]|bf16|[-50,100]|erf|49.9M|erf|\n52: |10|[2049,513]|f16|[-65504,65504]|tanh|1.05M|tanh|\n53: |11|[3,7,13,4001]|f32|[-88,88]|erf|1.09M|erf|\n54: |12|[1000003]|bf16|[-inf,inf]|tanh|1.00M|tanh|\n55: |13|[11,13,17,67,67]|f32|[nan,nan]|erf|10.9M|erf|\n56: |14|[3,7,11,13,1009]|f16|[0,0]|tanh|3.03M|tanh|\n57: |15|[512,2049]|f32|[-0.5,0.5]|erf|1.05M|erf|\n58: |16|[255,8193]|bf16|[-1,3]|erf|2.09M|erf|\n59: |17|[4097,511]|f16|[-1000,1000]|tanh|2.09M|tanh|\n60: |18|[2,511,2049]|f32|[-0.2,0.2]|erf|2.09M|erf|\n61: |19|[4,255,2049]|bf16|[-3,6]|tanh|2.09M|tanh|\n62: |20|[2,3,17,1024,101]|f32|[-20,40]|erf|10.5M|erf|\n63: \n64: All cases ≥ ~1.0M elems ⇒ all take the wide tile path; narrow path retained only for\n65: spec-completeness on tiny/empty tensors (`size == 0` → return `empty_like`).\n66: \n67: ## 4. Tiling & tails\n68: \n69: Two kernels (separate JIT cache entries, minimal UB per path):\n70: `_gelu_erf_kernel` and `_gelu_tanh_kernel`, each grid-stride:\n71: \n72: ```\n73: for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2):\n74:     off = t * tile\n75:     n = tile if off + tile <= size else size - off     # tail\n76:     x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile], real_shape=[n])\n77:     xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n78:     ...compute yf in f32...\n79:     asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n80: ```\n81: \n82: Tiles (pinned, see §5):\n83: - `_ERF_TILE  = 2048` (wide), `_NARROW = 1024`.\n84: - `_TANH_TILE = 1024` (wide == narrow; tanh chain is longer).\n85: - `_MAX_CORES = 72`; threshold `_MAX_CORES * _ERF_TILE = 147456`.\n86: \n87: Dispatch:\n88: - `size == 0` → `return torch.empty_like(x)`.\n89: - erf: `size >= threshold` → TILE=2048 else 1024; `cores=min(72, ceildiv(size,TILE))`.\n90: - tanh: TILE=1024 always; `cores=min(72, ceildiv(size,1024))`.\n91: \n92: ## 5. UB budget (253952 B, static alloc)\n93: \n94: Formula (measured calibration from the sigmoid reference on this build): \n95: `real ≈ 1.6 * V * 4 * TILE * unroll(=2)`, where `V` = #live f32 tile values.\n96: \n97: - **erf chain** `V ≈ 6` (`xf, s, e, one, hx, y`) + input-dtype load/store.\n98:   erf@2048 u2: `1.6*6*4*2048*2 = 157286 B` ✓ (96 KB headroom; matches the proven\n99:   sigmoid chain length, and gives margin for any hidden erf temporaries).\n100: - **tanh chain** `V ≈ 10` (`xf, x2, x3, a, b, c, t, one, hx, y`).\n101:   tanh@2048 u2: `1.6*10*4*2048*2 = 262144 B` ✗ (8 KB over ⇒ launch-time `UB overflow`).\n102:   tanh@1536 u2: `1.6*10*4*1536*2 = 196608 B` ✓ (57 KB / 23% headroom).\n103:   tanh@1024 u2: `1.6*10*4*1024*2 = 131072 B` ✓ (122 KB headroom).\n104:   **Pinned: tanh TILE = 1024** — chosen for one-shot safety (no local NPU to probe\n105:   hidden temporaries of the `tanh`/`mul` chain); 1536 is a perf fallback if a local\n106:   compile gate were available. UB overflow is a **runtime** launch failure (not caught\n107:   by the exact-v2 compile gate), so conservative is correct here.\n108: \n109: 256-byte alignment rule: `TILE*4 % 256 == 0` ⇒ `TILE % 64 == 0`; 2048 and 1024 both OK.\n110: \n111: ## 6. Numerical risks\n112: \n113: - **x³ overflow**: max |x| in tanh cases is 65504 (case 10, f16→f32). `65504³ ≈ 2.8e14`,\n114:   well within f32 (max ~3.4e38). case 17 (±1000) → 1e9. No overflow.\n115: - **tanh saturation**: `tanh(large)=±1`; for large |x|, `K*x³` dominates, `x` is lost in\n116:   `x + K*x³` (catastrophic cancellation) **but** tanh has already saturated to ±1, so\n117:   `y = 0.5*x*(±1+1) = x or 0` — the cancellation is benign and matches golden, which\n118:   uses the identical formula. No special-case branch.\n119: - **erf saturation**: `erf(|x|/√2)`→±1 for |x|≳6 (cases 9,11,20). `asc2.erf` is a vector\n120:   op on this build; saturation gives correct limits `y→x` (+∞), `y→0` (−∞).\n121: - **Inf (case 12 bf16 [−inf,inf])**: IEEE propagation — `x=+inf ⇒ x³=inf ⇒ c=inf ⇒\n122:   tanh=1 ⇒ y=+inf`; `x=−inf ⇒ c=−inf ⇒ tanh=−1 ⇒ 0.5*(−inf)*0 = NaN`. Golden\n123:   (`torch.nn.functional.gelu`) computes the same expression and yields the same IEEE\n124:   result ⇒ relative-error match (golden-equal). Documented as a residual `suspected`\n125:   risk if the harness treats `NaN≠NaN`; cannot be special-cased without diverging from\n126:   golden.\n127: - **NaN (case 13 f32 [nan,nan])**: `erf(NaN)=NaN`, `0.5*NaN*(1+NaN)=NaN`. IEEE\n128:   propagation through `asc2.erf`/mul ⇒ matches golden. Same residual NaN-comparison\n129:   caveat as above.\n130: - **Zero (case 14 [0,0] tanh)**: `erf/tanh(0)=0`, `y=0`. Exact.\n131: - **Precision**: f16 thresh `2^-10≈9.7e-4`, bf16 `2^-7≈7.8e-3`, f32 `2^-13≈1.2e-4`.\n132:   All f16/bf16 cases compute in f32 then cast back ⇒ strictly more accurate than the\n133:   golden's f16/bf16 path; f32 cases use the cancellation-free erf/tanh forms with no\n134:   `exp(+arg)` (no overflow) and no `log(1+tiny)` (no flush). `erf`/`tanh` are bounded,\n135:   so no guard-band logic is needed.\n136: \n137: ## 7. Anti-cheat constraints\n138: \n139: - ALL math (`erf`, `tanh`, `*`, `+`, casts) lives inside `@asc2.jit` kernels launched on\n140:   the NPU. Host does only: `ensure_npu_platform()`, `.contiguous()`, `torch.empty_like`,\n141:   `.numel()`, `.dtype`, string dispatch, launch, return.\n142: - No torch compute/math ops anywhere (`torch.mul`, `F.gelu`, `a+b`, `.to(dtype)` on\n143:   device data, `torch.cat/clone/sum`, `x.sigmoid()`…). No `data_ptr` caching.\n144: - `approximate` string is consumed on the host only (never passed into a kernel — str\n145:   is not a supported param type anyway).\n146: - Output is a fresh contiguous NPU tensor (`torch.empty_like(x)`) with golden's exact\n147:   shape/dtype; no views of the input.\n148: - Constants precomputed module-level; no `import`/`math.*` inside jit.\n149: \n150: ## 8. Local validation ladder\n151: \n152: No NPU and no pyasc/asc/asc2/torch_npu installed locally (per task.md). Ladder:\n153: \n154: 1. **Syntax only** — `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` (allowed; checks AST, no\n155:    imports execute). Run after writing candidate.\n156: 2. **Worker static contract check** — requires the CANNBench worker runtime; not\n157:    runnable here ⇒ treated as `suspected`, deferred to remote.\n158: 3. **Exact-v2 local compile gate** (skill `references/local-validation.md`) — requires\n159:    the pinned `pyasc-v2-source`; not installed here ⇒ `suspected`, deferred. UB\n160:    overflow (§5) is a runtime launch failure that this gate would NOT catch anyway;\n161:    the conservative tiles in §4 are chosen to avoid it a priori.\n162: 4. **camodel numerical compare vs golden.py** — no local camodel ⇒ `suspected`.\n163: 5. **CANNBench on real NPU** — the only acceptance/performance oracle; remote, invoked\n164:    by the official harness.\n165: \n166: Evidence label for the design phase: `suspected` (no local compile/numerical evidence\n167: possible). Promotion to `verified-local-compile` / `verified-camodel` requires steps\n168: 2–4, which are unavailable in this environment.\n169: \n170: ## 9. Open implementation notes (for candidate.py, next phase)\n171: \n172: - Two kernels: `_gelu_erf_kernel` and `_gelu_tanh_kernel`, identical signature\n173:   `(x: asc.GlobalAddress, out: asc.GlobalAddress, size: int, num_tiles: int,\n174:    tile: asc.ConstExpr[int])`.\n175: - Host `gelu(x, approximate=\"none\")`: `ensure_npu_platform()`; `if not x.is_contiguous():\n176:   x = x.contiguous()`; `out = torch.empty_like(x)`; `size = x.numel()`; empty→return;\n177:   branch on `approximate` (`\"none\"`→erf, `\"tanh\"`→tanh; any other value ⇒ assert, since\n178:   spec allows only these two); pick tile per §4; `ceildiv` via `asc.ceildiv`;\n179:   `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`; launch; return `out`.\n180: - `x.is_contiguous()` / `.contiguous()` / `.numel()` / `.dtype` are metadata/views —\n181:   allowed by the anti-cheat whitelist.\n182: \n183: DESIGN_DONE\n\n(End of file - total 183 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# design.md — Gelu (CANNBench, pyasc asc2)\n\nProvenance: skills `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` + `pyasc-syntax-constraints` loaded; context\n= `task.md` (desc/proto/golden/20 cases + kernel contract) only. No submission modules,\nrun artifacts, or pyasc source inspected. `candidate.py` not yet written.\n\n## 1. Algorithm\n\nPublic callable `gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n`approximate` is a **str** → unsupported as a kernel param (type constraints).\nDispatch on the host string and launch one of two specialized `@asc2.jit` kernels.\nBoth kernels flatten to 1-D (`numel`), promote f16/bf16→f32, compute, cast back.\n\n- **erf mode** (`approximate == \"none\"`): `y = (x*0.5) * (erf(x*C1) + 1.0)`,\n  `C1 = 1/sqrt(2) = 0.7071067811865476`.\n- **tanh mode** (`approximate == \"tanh\"`):\n  `y = (x*0.5) * (tanh(C0 * (x + K*x*x*x)) + 1.0)`,\n  `C0 = sqrt(2/pi) = 0.7978845608028654`, `K = 0.044715`.\n  Compute order: `x2=x*x; x3=x2*x; a=x3*K; b=x+a; c=b*C0; t=tanh(c); one=t+1.0; hx=x*0.5; y=hx*one`.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/design.md","text":"# design.md — Gelu (CANNBench, pyasc asc2)\n\nProvenance: skills `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` + `pyasc-syntax-constraints` loaded; context\n= `task.md` (desc/proto/golden/20 cases + kernel contract) only. No submission modules,\nrun artifacts, or pyasc source inspected. `candidate.py` not yet written.\n\n## 1. Algorithm\n\nPublic callable `gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n`approximate` is a **str** → unsupported as a kernel param (type constraints).\nDispatch on the host string and launch one of two specialized `@asc2.jit` kernels.\nBoth kernels flatten to 1-D (`numel`), promote f16/bf16→f32, compute, cast back.\n\n- **erf mode** (`approximate == \"none\"`): `y = (x*0.5) * (erf(x*C1) + 1.0)`,\n  `C1 = 1/sqrt(2) = 0.7071067811865476`.\n- **tanh mode** (`approximate == \"tanh\"`):\n  `y = (x*0.5) * (tanh(C0 * (x + K*x*x*x)) + 1.0)`,\n  `C0 = sqrt(2/pi) = 0.7978845608028654`, `K = 0.044715`.\n  Compute order: `x2=x*x; x3=x2*x; a=x3*K; b=x+a; c=b*C0; t=tanh(c); one=t+1.0; hx=x*0.5; y=hx*one`.\n\nAll constants are module-level floats (no `math.*` inside jit). Scalars always on the\nRIGHT of tile arithmetic (`x*C1`, `t+1.0`, `x*0.5`) — `Tile.__rmul__` is absent.\n\n## 2. Pinned v2 APIs (CANNBench contract)\n\n- `from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform`\n- `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` — 1-D GM view (rank-1 throughout; no 2-D mix).\n- `asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile], real_shape=[n])` — tile load with tail.\n- `asc2.copy_out(y_cast, out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])` — tile store with tail.\n- `asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2)` — grid-stride.\n- `asc.GlobalAddress` for ptrs; `int` for size/num_tiles; `asc.ConstExpr[int]` for tile size.\n- Casts: `x.to(asc.float32)`, `y.to(x.dtype)`. Math: `asc2.erf`, `asc2.tanh`, `+ *`.\n- Launch: `kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, TILE)` with `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`.\n- Target: `Ascend950PR_9599`, 72 AIV cores, UB 253952 B.\n\n## 3. All 20 cases (coverage)\n\n1-D flatten + grid-stride + `real_shape` tails covers every rank (1D–5D present;\nspec 0–8D) and every odd/non-multiple shape. No host shape branch needed.\n\n| # | shape | dtype | range | mode | elems | path |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|1|[1024,1024]|f16|[-1,1]|erf|1.05M|erf|\n|2|[2048,2048]|f32|[-2,2]|erf|4.19M|erf|\n|3|[4096,4096]|bf16|[-3,3]|erf|16.78M|erf|\n|4|[8192,8192]|f16|[-10,10]|tanh|67.1M|tanh|\n|5|[8192,8192]|f32|[-100,100]|tanh|67.1M|tanh|\n|6|[1023,1023]|bf16|[-0.1,0.1]|tanh|1.05M|tanh|\n|7|[1009,1021]|f16|[-1,2]|erf|1.03M|erf|\n|8|[1537,769]|f32|[-5,10]|tanh|1.18M|tanh|\n|9|[363,367,373]|bf16|[-50,100]|erf|49.9M|erf|\n|10|[2049,513]|f16|[-65504,65504]|tanh|1.05M|tanh|\n|11|[3,7,13,4001]|f32|[-88,88]|erf|1.09M|erf|\n|12|[1000003]|bf16|[-inf,inf]|tanh|1.00M|tanh|\n|13|[11,13,17,67,67]|f32|[nan,nan]|erf|10.9M|erf|\n|14|[3,7,11,13,1009]|f16|[0,0]|tanh|3.03M|tanh|\n|15|[512,2049]|f32|[-0.5,0.5]|erf|1.05M|erf|\n|16|[255,8193]|bf16|[-1,3]|erf|2.09M|erf|\n|17|[4097,511]|f16|[-1000,1000]|tanh|2.09M|tanh|\n|18|[2,511,2049]|f32|[-0.2,0.2]|erf|2.09M|erf|\n|19|[4,255,2049]|bf16|[-3,6]|tanh|2.09M|tanh|\n|20|[2,3,17,1024,101]|f32|[-20,40]|erf|10.5M|erf|\n\nAll cases ≥ ~1.0M elems ⇒ all take the wide tile path; narrow path retained only for\nspec-completeness on tiny/empty tensors (`size == 0` → return `empty_like`).\n\n## 4. Tiling & tails\n\nTwo kernels (separate JIT cache entries, minimal UB per path):\n`_gelu_erf_kernel` and `_gelu_tanh_kernel`, each grid-stride:\n\n```\nfor t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2):\n    off = t * tile\n    n = tile if off + tile <= size else size - off     # tail\n    x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile], real_shape=[n])\n    xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n    ...compute yf in f32...\n    asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n```\n\nTiles (pinned, see §5):\n- `_ERF_TILE  = 2048` (wide), `_NARROW = 1024`.\n- `_TANH_TILE = 1024` (wide == narrow; tanh chain is longer).\n- `_MAX_CORES = 72`; threshold `_MAX_CORES * _ERF_TILE = 147456`.\n\nDispatch:\n- `size == 0` → `return torch.empty_like(x)`.\n- erf: `size >= threshold` → TILE=2048 else 1024; `cores=min(72, ceildiv(size,TILE))`.\n- tanh: TILE=1024 always; `cores=min(72, ceildiv(size,1024))`.\n\n## 5. UB budget (253952 B, static alloc)\n\nFormula (measured calibration from the sigmoid reference on this build): \n`real ≈ 1.6 * V * 4 * TILE * unroll(=2)`, where `V` = #live f32 tile values.\n\n- **erf chain** `V ≈ 6` (`xf, s, e, one, hx, y`) + input-dtype load/store.\n  erf@2048 u2: `1.6*6*4*2048*2 = 157286 B` ✓ (96 KB headroom; matches the proven\n  sigmoid chain length, and gives margin for any hidden erf temporaries).\n- **tanh chain** `V ≈ 10` (`xf, x2, x3, a, b, c, t, one, hx, y`).\n  tanh@2048 u2: `1.6*10*4*2048*2 = 262144 B` ✗ (8 KB over ⇒ launch-time `UB overflow`).\n  tanh@1536 u2: `1.6*10*4*1536*2 = 196608 B` ✓ (57 KB / 23% headroom).\n  tanh@1024 u2: `1.6*10*4*1024*2 = 131072 B` ✓ (122 KB headroom).\n  **Pinned: tanh TILE = 1024** — chosen for one-shot safety (no local NPU to probe\n  hidden temporaries of the `tanh`/`mul` chain); 1536 is a perf fallback if a local\n  compile gate were available. UB overflow is a **runtime** launch failure (not caught\n  by the exact-v2 compile gate), so conservative is correct here.\n\n256-byte alignment rule: `TILE*4 % 256 == 0` ⇒ `TILE % 64 == 0`; 2048 and 1024 both OK.\n\n## 6. Numerical risks\n\n- **x³ overflow**: max |x| in tanh cases is 65504 (case 10, f16→f32). `65504³ ≈ 2.8e14`,\n  well within f32 (max ~3.4e38). case 17 (±1000) → 1e9. No overflow.\n- **tanh saturation**: `tanh(large)=±1`; for large |x|, `K*x³` dominates, `x` is lost in\n  `x + K*x³` (catastrophic cancellation) **but** tanh has already saturated to ±1, so\n  `y = 0.5*x*(±1+1) = x or 0` — the cancellation is benign and matches golden, which\n  uses the identical formula. No special-case branch.\n- **erf saturation**: `erf(|x|/√2)`→±1 for |x|≳6 (cases 9,11,20). `asc2.erf` is a vector\n  op on this build; saturation gives correct limits `y→x` (+∞), `y→0` (−∞).\n- **Inf (case 12 bf16 [−inf,inf])**: IEEE propagation — `x=+inf ⇒ x³=inf ⇒ c=inf ⇒\n  tanh=1 ⇒ y=+inf`; `x=−inf ⇒ c=−inf ⇒ tanh=−1 ⇒ 0.5*(−inf)*0 = NaN`. Golden\n  (`torch.nn.functional.gelu`) computes the same expression and yields the same IEEE\n  result ⇒ relative-error match (golden-equal). Documented as a residual `suspected`\n  risk if the harness treats `NaN≠NaN`; cannot be special-cased without diverging from\n  golden.\n- **NaN (case 13 f32 [nan,nan])**: `erf(NaN)=NaN`, `0.5*NaN*(1+NaN)=NaN`. IEEE\n  propagation through `asc2.erf`/mul ⇒ matches golden. Same residual NaN-comparison\n  caveat as above.\n- **Zero (case 14 [0,0] tanh)**: `erf/tanh(0)=0`, `y=0`. Exact.\n- **Precision**: f16 thresh `2^-10≈9.7e-4`, bf16 `2^-7≈7.8e-3`, f32 `2^-13≈1.2e-4`.\n  All f16/bf16 cases compute in f32 then cast back ⇒ strictly more accurate than the\n  golden's f16/bf16 path; f32 cases use the cancellation-free erf/tanh forms with no\n  `exp(+arg)` (no overflow) and no `log(1+tiny)` (no flush). `erf`/`tanh` are bounded,\n  so no guard-band logic is needed.\n\n## 7. Anti-cheat constraints\n\n- ALL math (`erf`, `tanh`, `*`, `+`, casts) lives inside `@asc2.jit` kernels launched on\n  the NPU. Host does only: `ensure_npu_platform()`, `.contiguous()`, `torch.empty_like`,\n  `.numel()`, `.dtype`, string dispatch, launch, return.\n- No torch compute/math ops anywhere (`torch.mul`, `F.gelu`, `a+b`, `.to(dtype)` on\n  device data, `torch.cat/clone/sum`, `x.sigmoid()`…). No `data_ptr` caching.\n- `approximate` string is consumed on the host only (never passed into a kernel — str\n  is not a supported param type anyway).\n- Output is a fresh contiguous NPU tensor (`torch.empty_like(x)`) with golden's exact\n  shape/dtype; no views of the input.\n- Constants precomputed module-level; no `import`/`math.*` inside jit.\n\n## 8. Local validation ladder\n\nNo NPU and no pyasc/asc/asc2/torch_npu installed locally (per task.md). Ladder:\n\n1. **Syntax only** — `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` (allowed; checks AST, no\n   imports execute). Run after writing candidate.\n2. **Worker static contract check** — requires the CANNBench worker runtime; not\n   runnable here ⇒ treated as `suspected`, deferred to remote.\n3. **Exact-v2 local compile gate** (skill `references/local-validation.md`) — requires\n   the pinned `pyasc-v2-source`; not installed here ⇒ `suspected`, deferred. UB\n   overflow (§5) is a runtime launch failure that this gate would NOT catch anyway;\n   the conservative tiles in §4 are chosen to avoid it a priori.\n4. **camodel numerical compare vs golden.py** — no local camodel ⇒ `suspected`.\n5. **CANNBench on real NPU** — the only acceptance/performance oracle; remote, invoked\n   by the official harness.\n\nEvidence label for the design phase: `suspected` (no local compile/numerical evidence\npossible). Promotion to `verified-local-compile` / `verified-camodel` requires steps\n2–4, which are unavailable in this environment.\n\n## 9. Open implementation notes (for candidate.py, next phase)\n\n- Two kernels: `_gelu_erf_kernel` and `_gelu_tanh_kernel`, identical signature\n  `(x: asc.GlobalAddress, out: asc.GlobalAddress, size: int, num_tiles: int,\n   tile: asc.ConstExpr[int])`.\n- Host `gelu(x, approximate=\"none\")`: `ensure_npu_platform()`; `if not x.is_contiguous():\n  x = x.contiguous()`; `out = torch.empty_like(x)`; `size = x.numel()`; empty→return;\n  branch on `approximate` (`\"none\"`→erf, `\"tanh\"`→tanh; any other value ⇒ assert, since\n  spec allows only these two); pick tile per §4; `ceildiv` via `asc.ceildiv`;\n  `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`; launch; return `out`.\n- `x.is_contiguous()` / `.contiguous()` / `.numel()` / `.dtype` are metadata/views —\n  allowed by the anti-cheat whitelist.\n\nDESIGN_DONE","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":183,"totalLines":183,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/design.md","time":{"start":1788374346497,"end":1788374346502}},"id":"prt_0636ae886001MNCgJ1r2L72aSY","sessionID":"ses_f9c952882ffeAnIEP58bPaIy7l","messageID":"msg_0636ad84c001qK5pwkwH9hce0x"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788374347166,"sessionID":"ses_f9c952882ffeAnIEP58bPaIy7l","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_2462468b02e64d45b7cc9dba","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/candidate.py"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/candidate.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"CANN Bench Gelu interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n2: \n3: Kernel design (grid-stride variant):\n4:   - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count / rank works.\n5:   - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n6:   - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision (the\n7:     spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute), then cast back on\n8:     store.\n9:   - Host dispatches on the ``approximate`` string (unsupported as a kernel\n10:     param) to one of two specialized ``@asc2.jit`` kernels:\n11:       * erf mode  (approximate == \"none\"):\n12:             y = (x * 0.5) * (erf(x / sqrt(2)) + 1.0)\n13:       * tanh mode (approximate == \"tanh\"):\n14:             y = (x * 0.5) * (tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)) + 1.0)\n15:   - All constants are module-level floats (no math.* inside jit); scalars stay\n16:     on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no __rmul__).\n17:   - Tiles: erf chain (V~6) uses 2048 wide / 1024 narrow; tanh chain (V~10) uses\n18:     1024 (UB-budget safe under 253952 B with unroll_factor=2).\n19:   - erf/tanh are bounded ops, so no overflow guard is needed; IEEE special\n20:     values (Inf/NaN) propagate through the vector ops and match the golden's\n21:     identical-form evaluation.\n22: \"\"\"\n23: \n24: import math\n25: \n26: import torch\n27: \n28: import asc\n29: import asc2\n30: \n31: from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n32: \n33: _C1_ERF = 1.0 / math.sqrt(2.0)\n34: _C0_TANH = 2.0 * math.sqrt(2.0 / math.pi)\n35: _K_TANH = 0.044715\n36: \n37: _ERF_TILE = 2048\n38: _NARROW_TILE = 1024\n39: _TANH_TILE = 1024\n40: _MAX_CORES = 72\n41: _ERF_THRESHOLD = _MAX_CORES * _ERF_TILE\n42: \n43: \n44: @asc2.jit\n45: def _gelu_erf_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n46:                      size: int, num_tiles: int,\n47:                      tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n48:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n49:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n50:     for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n51:                         unroll_factor=2):\n52:         off = t * tile_size\n53:         n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n54:         x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n55:         xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n56:         z = asc2.abs(xf) * _C1_ERF\n57:         t = 1.0 / (1.0 + 0.5 * z)\n58:         p = t * 0.17087277 - 0.82215223\n59:         p = p * t + 1.48851587\n60:         p = p * t - 1.13520398\n61:         p = p * t + 0.27886807\n62:         p = p * t - 0.18628806\n63:         p = p * t + 0.09678418\n64:         p = p * t + 0.37409196\n65:         p = p * t + 1.00002368\n66:         p = p * t - 1.26551223\n67:         efc = t * asc2.exp(p - z * z)\n68:         hxh = xf * 0.5 * efc\n69:         neg = xf - hxh\n70:         yf = asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, neg, hxh)\n71:         asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n72: \n73: \n74: @asc2.jit\n75: def _gelu_tanh_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n76:                       size: int, num_tiles: int,\n77:                       tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n78:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n79:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n80:     for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n81:                         unroll_factor=2):\n82:         off = t * tile_size\n83:         n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n84:         x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n85:         xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n86:         x2 = xf * xf\n87:         x3 = x2 * xf\n88:         s = (xf + x3 * _K_TANH) * _C0_TANH\n89:         em = asc2.exp(asc2.minimum(s, 0.0))\n90:         ea = asc2.exp(-asc2.abs(s))\n91:         yf = xf * em / (1.0 + ea)\n92:         asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n93: \n94: \n95: def gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor:\n96:     \"\"\"Element-wise GELU of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n97:     ensure_npu_platform()\n98:     assert approximate in (\"none\", \"tanh\"), (\n99:         f\"approximate must be 'none' or 'tanh', got {approximate!r}\")\n100:     if not x.is_contiguous():\n101:         x = x.contiguous()\n102:     out = torch.empty_like(x)\n103:     size = x.numel()\n104:     if size == 0:\n105:         return out\n106:     if approximate == \"none\":\n107:         if size >= _ERF_THRESHOLD:\n108:             tile = _ERF_TILE\n109:         else:\n110:             tile = _NARROW_TILE\n111:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n112:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n113:         _gelu_erf_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n114:     else:\n115:         tile = _TANH_TILE\n116:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n117:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n118:         _gelu_tanh_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n119:     return out\n\n(End of file - total 119 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"CANN Bench Gelu interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n\nKernel design (grid-stride variant):\n  - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count / rank works.\n  - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n  - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision (the\n    spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute), then cast back on\n    store.\n  - Host dispatches on the ``approximate`` string (unsupported as a kernel\n    param) to one of two specialized ``@asc2.jit`` kernels:\n      * erf mode  (approximate == \"none\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (erf(x / sqrt(2)) + 1.0)\n      * tanh mode (approximate == \"tanh\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)) + 1.0)\n  - All constants are module-level floats (no math.* inside jit); scalars stay\n    on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no __rmul__).\n  - Tiles: erf chain (V~6) uses 2048 wide / 1024 narrow; tanh chain (V~10) uses\n    1024 (UB-budget safe under 253952 B with unroll_factor=2).\n  - erf/tanh are bounded ops, so no overflow guard is needed; IEEE special\n    values (Inf/NaN) propagate through the vector ops and match the golden's","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/candidate.py","text":"\"\"\"CANN Bench Gelu interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n\nKernel design (grid-stride variant):\n  - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count / rank works.\n  - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n  - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision (the\n    spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute), then cast back on\n    store.\n  - Host dispatches on the ``approximate`` string (unsupported as a kernel\n    param) to one of two specialized ``@asc2.jit`` kernels:\n      * erf mode  (approximate == \"none\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (erf(x / sqrt(2)) + 1.0)\n      * tanh mode (approximate == \"tanh\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)) + 1.0)\n  - All constants are module-level floats (no math.* inside jit); scalars stay\n    on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no __rmul__).\n  - Tiles: erf chain (V~6) uses 2048 wide / 1024 narrow; tanh chain (V~10) uses\n    1024 (UB-budget safe under 253952 B with unroll_factor=2).\n  - erf/tanh are bounded ops, so no overflow guard is needed; IEEE special\n    values (Inf/NaN) propagate through the vector ops and match the golden's\n    identical-form evaluation.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport math\n\nimport torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc2\n\nfrom ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n\n_C1_ERF = 1.0 / math.sqrt(2.0)\n_C0_TANH = 2.0 * math.sqrt(2.0 / math.pi)\n_K_TANH = 0.044715\n\n_ERF_TILE = 2048\n_NARROW_TILE = 1024\n_TANH_TILE = 1024\n_MAX_CORES = 72\n_ERF_THRESHOLD = _MAX_CORES * _ERF_TILE\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _gelu_erf_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                     size: int, num_tiles: int,\n                     tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size\n        n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n        x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n        xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n        z = asc2.abs(xf) * _C1_ERF\n        t = 1.0 / (1.0 + 0.5 * z)\n        p = t * 0.17087277 - 0.82215223\n        p = p * t + 1.48851587\n        p = p * t - 1.13520398\n        p = p * t + 0.27886807\n        p = p * t - 0.18628806\n        p = p * t + 0.09678418\n        p = p * t + 0.37409196\n        p = p * t + 1.00002368\n        p = p * t - 1.26551223\n        efc = t * asc2.exp(p - z * z)\n        hxh = xf * 0.5 * efc\n        neg = xf - hxh\n        yf = asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, neg, hxh)\n        asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _gelu_tanh_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                      size: int, num_tiles: int,\n                      tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size\n        n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n        x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n        xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n        x2 = xf * xf\n        x3 = x2 * xf\n        s = (xf + x3 * _K_TANH) * _C0_TANH\n        em = asc2.exp(asc2.minimum(s, 0.0))\n        ea = asc2.exp(-asc2.abs(s))\n        yf = xf * em / (1.0 + ea)\n        asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n\n\ndef gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"Element-wise GELU of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n    ensure_npu_platform()\n    assert approximate in (\"none\", \"tanh\"), (\n        f\"approximate must be 'none' or 'tanh', got {approximate!r}\")\n    if not x.is_contiguous():\n        x = x.contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    size = x.numel()\n    if size == 0:\n        return out\n    if approximate == \"none\":\n        if size >= _ERF_THRESHOLD:\n            tile = _ERF_TILE\n        else:\n            tile = _NARROW_TILE\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _gelu_erf_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n    else:\n        tile = _TANH_TILE\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _gelu_tanh_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n    return out","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":119,"totalLines":119,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/candidate.py","time":{"start":1788374347160,"end":1788374347165}},"id":"prt_0636aeb6a0016iLY6OT56SnChC","sessionID":"ses_f9c952882ffeAnIEP58bPaIy7l","messageID":"msg_0636ad84c001qK5pwkwH9hce0x"}}
